\plain\plain\f0\fs22\ql\plain\f0\fs22\plain\f1\fs22 Chief complaint: Follow-up for acid reflux, concern for nevus and a lump on the head\par 
\par 
HPI: \par 
Acid reflux-patient mentioned that he has a persistent symptoms of heartburn, usually have a regurgitation of the nonacidic fluid once a month.  Has tried PPI in the past for a month and never received complete relief of the symptoms.  Not interested 
in trying any further medication.  He request further work-up of why he has a acid reflux, and would like to see a specialist.\par 
Has noticed a mole on his right palm for the last 6 months.\par 
Also has a swelling/lump on the left side of the head which is not tender but is wondering if there is anything to worry about it.\par 
\par 
